values ('ap_biology', 3, '3.4', array['3.4']::text[], 'list_sequence', 'Light reactions: electron and proton flow', 'Order of events in the light reactions of photosynthesis in the thylakoid membrane.', '[{"label": "1", "meaning": "Chlorophylls absorb light energy, boosting electrons to a higher energy level in photosystems I and II"}, {"label": "2", "meaning": "Water splits, supplying electrons to replace those lost from photosystem II"}, {"label": "3", "meaning": "Electrons pass through the ETC connecting photosystems II and I in oxidation/reduction reactions"}, {"label": "4", "meaning": "A proton gradient forms across the thylakoid membrane (high inside, low outside)"}, {"label": "5", "meaning": "Electrons are ultimately transferred to NADP+, reducing it to NADPH in photosystem I"}, {"label": "6", "meaning": "Protons flow back through ATP synthase (chemiosmosis), forming ATP from ADP and inorganic phosphate (photophosphorylation)"}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-biology-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_biology-u3-r1-017; ced=3.4.B.2–3.4.B.5 — "Water then splits, supplying electrons to replace those lost from photosystem II"')
